            {
                "entry_id": "53e2c14a-b1e1-3b92-809a-80ea35c153ac",
                "word": "Kool-Aid",
                "pos": "noun",
                "lang_code": "en",
                "forms": [
                    {
                        "form_id": "c5585c8a-0a45-4606-ac55-41a9fba0f3c7",
                        "entry_id": "53e2c14a-b1e1-3b92-809a-80ea35c153ac",
                        "tags": [
                            "plural"
                        ],
                        "form": "Kool-Aids"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "bdd642be-5f44-32a7-b6ec-b3a72d31c4d0",
                        "entry_id": "53e2c14a-b1e1-3b92-809a-80ea35c153ac",
                        "glosses": [
                            "A fad or ideology that is adopted unquestioningly, ignoring its hidden dangers or disadvantages."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "cbcdd0fb-8186-481e-91b9-f9100dc3c1d4",
                                "sense_id": "bdd642be-5f44-32a7-b6ec-b3a72d31c4d0",
                                "text": "The problem today isn't really with the Kool Aids; it's with society's refusal to distinguish between him and all the rest who fall into the hands of the system."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "17b6495d-0b90-4760-a48f-593c04ca65fa",
                                "sense_id": "bdd642be-5f44-32a7-b6ec-b3a72d31c4d0",
                                "text": "Pfizer reps departed training with a “Pass me the Kool-Aid” conviction that not only were our drugs the best in the industry, but also that our company was the best in the world."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "4a222e8b-88d5-48be-ab36-352e61df2c25",
                                "sense_id": "bdd642be-5f44-32a7-b6ec-b3a72d31c4d0",
                                "text": "Kids are force-fed the Kool-Aid while their skulls are still soft. They have no concept of rational thought and their parents drag them to a church and force them to learn mythology disguised as religious doctrine and try to sell it as fact."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "47835666-8c11-4b04-b616-89bcca9aa389",
                                "sense_id": "bdd642be-5f44-32a7-b6ec-b3a72d31c4d0",
                                "text": "Hopefully by now you are beginning to see how the Kool-Aid is made, realized it is not poison, and are thinking about taking a sip. You are ready to rush out, buy your first bitcoin, and cash in on the digital gold rush."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "8dda42db-9999-4bb4-9e9c-77cc78ca07dd",
                                "sense_id": "bdd642be-5f44-32a7-b6ec-b3a72d31c4d0",
                                "text": "Memorably referred to by Warren Buffet in early 2008 as the 'poetic justice' of 'toxic Kool-Aid' (Dabrowski 2008), the specific issue addressed by these initiatives was the value, valuation, and circulation of assets related to and derived from US sub-prime mortgages."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "397f5658-7175-4ab1-bebb-c35f6f7ce343",
                                "sense_id": "bdd642be-5f44-32a7-b6ec-b3a72d31c4d0",
                                "text": "Suitcases full of Kool-Aid seem to have been wheeled into Boris Johnson’s meeting with Tory MPs last night."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [],
                "word_linkages": []
            },
            {
                "entry_id": "6331a70c-3480-3f08-849e-8e51d063e783",
                "word": "kool-aid",
                "pos": "noun",
                "lang_code": "en",
                "forms": [
                    {
                        "form_id": "07a92337-22ba-4214-a0e5-f3229735bd90",
                        "entry_id": "6331a70c-3480-3f08-849e-8e51d063e783",
                        "tags": [
                            "plural"
                        ],
                        "form": "kool-aids"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "07750553-6b18-3e88-9fa4-cce3c16553d0",
                        "entry_id": "6331a70c-3480-3f08-849e-8e51d063e783",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Alternative form of Kool-Aid (unquestioned fad or ideology)."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "alt-of",
                            "alternative"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "66362aa4-8070-4901-9644-15352f9680e7",
                                "sense_id": "07750553-6b18-3e88-9fa4-cce3c16553d0",
                                "text": "All of you military vets that drank that kool-aid and voted for him - shame on you."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "43415395-1465-423a-bfa8-d4bad56677c8",
                                "sense_id": "07750553-6b18-3e88-9fa4-cce3c16553d0",
                                "text": "And don't believe everything you see or fall into this alluring trap. Step away from the kool-aid, don't drink, it is no good. The kool-aid looks sweet but it is bitter and poisonous. The dangers of influence does not stop at our career choices, clothing ensembles, hairstyles and religious decisions; the followers of celebrities or whomever they have chosen as their new source of life, impact every aspect of their being."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "5ec85910-3b88-4284-9540-27d19ff93212",
                                "sense_id": "07750553-6b18-3e88-9fa4-cce3c16553d0",
                                "text": "For half a decade, Silicon Valley turned into nothing less than a business world version of Jonestown. The kool-aid wasn't lethal. But it was very potent, and people were drinking it by the gallon."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
